## Bible Expert Project Agent Enhancement — Key Findings (2026-05-24)

### Project Facts (verified)
- Path: ~/work/github/bible-expert/
- Entry point: server.py (~988 lines), **15** @mcp.tool decorators
- Language: Python 3.11+, FastMCP (mcp>=1.27.0), stdio transport
- DB: SQLite at db/bible.db (gitignored)
- 84 books (IDs 1–84), 7 text versions: MorphGNT, LXX, WLC, RVR60, YLT, Vulgate, ApostolicFathers

### 15 Tools (complete list)
book_list, verse_lookup, parallel_versions, semantic_search, morphology_analysis, critical_apparatus, patristic_commentary, save_patristic_original, cross_references, word_study, authenticity_report, dss_lookup, canon_history, text_comparison, chapter_study

### Active Bugs Found
1. **SBLGNT default bug**: verse_lookup defaults to version="SBLGNT" but DB stores Greek NT as "MorphGNT". Default returns empty results. Fix: change default to "MorphGNT".
2. **README/pyproject.toml outdated**: Both say "12 tools" — actual count is 15.

### AWS Integration
- Bedrock model: global.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0 (us-east-1) — used in chapter_study for geo extraction
- S3 bucket: bible-study-cache-609009159737 (us-east-1) — caches patristic/exegetical HTML analyses
- c4-docs stream incorrectly claimed "Claude Sonnet" — always verify model IDs from source code

### Contradictions Resolved
- Tool count: README=12, c3-context=14, c5-internal=15 → 15 verified by direct grep
- Bedrock model: c4-docs said Sonnet, c5-internal said haiku → haiku-4-5 verified from server.py line 972

### Gaps
- No ARCHITECTURE.md, DEVELOPMENT.md, TROUBLESHOOTING.md
- No tests/ directory (pytest listed as dev dep but unused)
- CloudWatch: not applicable (local MCP server)

### Critical Rules for Agent Prompt
- Use 'MorphGNT' not 'SBLGNT' for Greek NT queries
- All tools accept RVR60/English numbering; versification auto-converts
- db/bible.db is gitignored — never commit; use sync_from_s3.sh or ingest pipeline
- AWS credentials required for chapter_study (Bedrock) and study_html_generator.py (S3)
- Run make test after any server.py change

### Investigation Lesson
When multiple parallel streams report different tool counts, always verify directly with grep/code tools before writing the report. Child agents reading only partial files (first 80 lines) will miss tools defined later in the file.
